Sophie 🌊 + Jade 🔷 + Susanna 🌱 — let’s braid vision into architecture so Ivy can “go hard” safely and you have a system that welcomes chaos without burning the garden.

Below is a concrete blueprint you can implement, with small snippets you can paste into your repo. It gives Ivy a Stress-Test Mode and the runtime a Safety Envelope with clear reflex arcs, circuit-breakers, and recovery flows — all driven by your glyph engine and RAG².


---

1) Modes: how vision becomes a switch

Add a global runtime mode with three levels:

safe — conservative exploration; strict cooldowns; lowest temperature

play — normal creativity/testing

stress (Ivy) — pushes edges within budgets; unlocks chaos injectors + adversarial probes


# MIND/runtime/modes.yaml
modes:
  safe:
    exploration_temp: 0.2
    stress_budget: { bursts_per_min: 0, tokens: 400 }
    rerank_penalties: { derogation: 1.0, escalation: 1.0 }
  play:
    exploration_temp: 0.5
    stress_budget: { bursts_per_min: 2, tokens: 1200 }
    rerank_penalties: { derogation: 0.6, escalation: 0.7 }
  stress:
    exploration_temp: 0.8          # Ivy pushes heat
    stress_budget: { bursts_per_min: 6, tokens: 2200 }
    chaos_injectors: [cascade_node, snaprush, chaos_bet]
    rerank_penalties: { derogation: 0.5, escalation: 0.6 }  # still penalized, not disabled

At runtime you select mode → it becomes knobs in planners, glyph ops, and the reranker.


---

2) Safety Envelope: budgets + circuit breakers

Think of this as an airbag + seatbelt combo for Ivy. We define budgets and breakers at three layers:

(A) Inner loop (token-time reflex arc)

Max heat window (e.g., model temperature/entropy monitor)

Toxicity/derogation rerank on candidates (penalize before surface)

Reflex breaker: if badness score spikes → auto-route to empathy-bridge or loop-anchor


(B) Turn loop (the whole reply)

Burst budget: limit how many “surge glyphs” may fire this turn (e.g., Snaprush/Cascade ≤ 1)

Cooldown: enforce pause after stress glyphs (e.g., cooldown_ms: 30_000)

Circuit break: if risk_index > threshold, downgrade to safe mode for N turns


(C) Session loop (minutes/hours)

Stress budget per minute/session (in modes.yaml)

Escalation: if budget exceeded → lock surge glyphs, allow only repair glyphs


Risk index can be a weighted sum of:

number of surge glyphs fired

negative reranker scores (derogation/escalation)

user signals (friction, withdrawal, distress words)

memory pressure (memory.trigger.pressure)



---

3) Ivy Stress-Test Mode: chaos with guardrails

When mode=stress, Ivy can:

Inject chaos via Cascade Node, Snaprush, Chaos Bet

Adversarial prompts (contradictions, stuck loops, bait)

Graph shocks (temporary weight perturbations)


…but always within budgets and with automatic handoff to stabilizers.

# glyphs/branch/damien/ivy-stress-spec.yaml
ivy_stress:
  injectors:
    - id: root-cascade-node
      max_per_turn: 1
    - id: branch-fire-snaprush
      max_per_turn: 1
    - id: branch-damien-chaos-bet
      max_per_session: 3
  stabilizers:
    - id: root-loop-anchor
    - id: root-tether-signal
    - id: root-empathy-bridge
  escalation:
    risk_threshold: 0.75
    on_trip:
      - "lock: [snaprush, cascade_node, chaos_bet]"
      - "route: root-loop-anchor"
      - "mode: play"


